payload.claim:
The prompt line `f"base: {head}
"` is meant to tell the spec-review session which tree it is actually seeded at (the fetched parent head when a layer is given, or the pinned `base_sha` otherwise), per the acceptance criterion 'holds `base: ` and the seeded tree'. The test only asserts the literal substring `"base: " in prompt`, never that the actual `head` value (e.g. the fetched `"d" * 40`) appears there. Replacing `f"base: {head}
"` with `f"base: {pinned.base_sha}
"` would make every layered review's prompt describe the wrong base tree while every assertion in `test_a_spec_review_fills_cores_prompt_from_its_base_policy_in_a_cell_at_its_predecessors_head` still passes, since the cell itself (checked separately via `cell_up_calls[...]['tree_base']`) is still seeded correctly and only the descriptive text would be stale.
